yieldT -- ONE RETURN, TWO MEANINGS (F-122, Tony 2026-09-24). A loop or IF fired DIRECTLY by fireLabelMethod YIELDS its
own label -- fireLabelMethod adopts the return as the label, and a body's value can be a live field; one run by an
OWNER (its label carries `deferred`) returns the VALUE, as before. Told apart by `deferred`; the clean split waits
for the crossover.
The pair, one process, both read by value: DIRECT -- a top-level do-while (unbraced: a braced body cannot sit inside code={ }, whose box closes at the first }); s2Y must read 3 (a value-return
here hands the live s2Y up to be adopted as DO's label, and s2Y loses its data). OWNER -- the same do-while as an
action's last statement; the action's value must read 3 (a label-return here gives gDO).
H7, measured at landing: forced to always return the value, DIRECT reads the tag s2Y; forced to always return the
label, OWNER reads gDO.
